messages:
kai: opened a small PR to add a 'fallback_status' column to the model catalog and a short SDK v4 snippet that shows per-request opt-out and variant priority. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/9733

sylvie: can we avoid the binary naming? 'fallback_status' could be one of [enabled, disabled, conditional]. helps for models that only support short contexts.

kai: agreed — switched to enum `enabled|disabled|conditional` in the PR. added a note that 'conditional' requires docs to list constraints (e.g., seq_limit, kv_cache_sensitive).

marc: please include a tiny SDK snippet that demonstrates `variant_priority` and `opt_out_fallback` at the call level. Ops asked for an explicit opt-out example.

kai: pasted snippet in PR body, short example below:

```js
// SDK v4: variant priority + per-request opt-out
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });

await client.generate({
  model: 'astra8b@2026-10-01',
  input: 'Draft a short product blurb',
  routing: {
    variant_priority: ['astra8b', 'astra8b-q4'],
    opt_out_fallback: false // set true to forbid fallback for this call
  }
});
```

sylvie: nice and compact. add one sentence about observability: when fallback fires the Console emits `routing.variant_switch` event with `from`/`to`/`reason`.

kai: added event note and linked to console events doc. docs-bot: please lint and run link-check on PR #9733.

docs-bot: Running checks: snippet-lint OK. Links OK. YAML check: model-catalog CSV updated; header added. No failures.

marc: LGTM. I'll merge once the tiny editorial nit in the PR body is fixed (change 'forbid' -> 'disable').

kai: fixed. merging. backported snippet into quickstart examples.

sylvie: I'll follow up with a short migration note for teams to add `fallback_status` to any model cards they own.

kai: thanks all. closing thread.
